Z||000004||88formula||07-04-2001||11:39 PM||||Don't lose hope in it yet. There was a guy at my work who had a Ford Ranger. Someone lit the interior on fire and it burned the headliner and seat. The dash was saved because someone put the fire out. The whole interior was charcoal black from the smoke and you couldn’t see through the windows. Somehow he totally cleaned the interior and replaced the headliner and seats and is still driving it. You can’t tell it was ever in a fire. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrgone||07-05-2001||12:22 AM||||ah, i hope its not too bad, a little wipe-down here a pine tree freshener there.... good as new!||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierohoho||07-05-2001||11:29 AM||||If it turns out to be just smoke/soot on the outside and it claens up OK here's what you could try for the interior smoke smell.<P>Call around to several dry cleaners and explain the situation. Some of them will have an air Ionizer or an Ozone machine they use to remove smells from clothing. <P>I've seen this done where they run an outlet from the machine into the car through a piece of cardboard masked over the open window, then the run the machine which pumps the Ions/Ozone into the car. <P>(not sure how long, if they do it they will know)<P>This will take care of the smell no problem. <P>So who told you that the shop owner had no insurance, did he? He might not want that money to go to you but into his pocket instead.<P>Good luck, keep us posted. I would also call a lawyer and see what he thinks, sounds like arson to me. Good luck, keep us posted.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000007||CanadianGT||07-05-2001||11:48 AM||||Thanks for the ideas everyone.<BR>I got the chance to go down to the shop last night with my dad.  All the power was out from the fire, and it was hard to see my car very well.  The garage door was open though and I was able to look over it somewhat however.  It appears that the damage is mainly smoke damage.  The inside is not all black, but is darker, and it really smells bad. I am going to go to  dry cleaners today or tommorow and ask if the provide that air ionzer service.  Does anyone know of a cleaners that does this?  The outside however is completely dark with soot, and the windows have this really dark sticky sooty stuff on them, that is near impossible to rub off. I have pictures of all this, but it was really dark in there so I am not sure how it will turn out .I will try to post them once developed.  We told the owner of the Garage that we are going to tow my car out of there Friday Morning, and if he say's no, that we will pay the money into court.  Maybe I should just pay the money into court anyways. I mean they scratched all my paint originally,  they have had the car for over 3 months, for what was supposed to be a  10 day job, and it still does not run properly and now they have a fire that completely changes the colour of my car and its smell!!  I think I gotta go read that story that Mr.Wittlief wrote earlier in this thread, so I can keep my cool about this entire situation!  Hopefully some good comes of all this!<BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierobaby||07-05-2001||11:54 AM||||Kyle,<P>I am sooo sorry to hear about your car...personally I say screw the dumb gagrage guys Tow your car it is yours soot and all... and good luck cleaning it may take a while...but you can do it! once the dry cleaners are done...go get febreeze...its line a white bottle int he cleaning aisle that should make sure the smell doesn't come back!<P>------------------<BR>1984 Sweet Candy Apple red Fiero sport coupe :-D<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrgone||07-05-2001||10:54 PM||||febreeze rocks!  if you dont get the automotive febreeze stuff it will leave little white spots that come off with water.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">   <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B>||||reg||1
